Enable forwarding of TSO frames toward a TSO-capable egress.

ip_output() has passed oversized frames whose csum_flags intersect
the egress interface's CSUM_TSO hwassist since the vxlan work, and
pf_route() implements the same exemption, but the tryforward fast
paths and the IPv6 slow path still balk on a bare MTU comparison
and consume the packet with an ICMP error.  A TSO frame originated
behind an if_pair(4)/vxlan(4)-style interface therefore dies at the
first forwarding hop.  Mirror ip_output()'s exemption in all three
places: the egress interface has declared it will split the frame.

Written for FreeBSD 15.1; apply from /usr/src with:
  patch -p0 < routed-tso-forwarding.patch

--- sys/netinet/ip_fastfwd.c	2026-08-26 16:09:23.218781000 +0200
+++ sys/netinet/ip_fastfwd.c	2026-08-26 16:09:30.265488000 +0200
@@ -491,7 +491,9 @@
 	/*
 	 * Check if packet fits MTU or if hardware will fragment for us
 	 */
-	if (ip_len <= nh->nh_mtu) {
+	if (ip_len <= nh->nh_mtu ||
+	    (m->m_pkthdr.csum_flags & nh->nh_ifp->if_hwassist &
+	    (CSUM_TSO | CSUM_INNER_TSO)) != 0) {
 		/*
 		 * Avoid confusing lower layers.
 		 */
--- sys/netinet6/ip6_fastfwd.c	2026-08-26 16:09:23.222242000 +0200
+++ sys/netinet6/ip6_fastfwd.c	2026-08-26 16:09:56.782176000 +0200
@@ -207,7 +207,9 @@
 		goto dropin;
